hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5776","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most hateful of men to God is the most bitter adversary.”"
"5777","Ahmad bin Amr told us, he said: I am bin Wahb, he said: Malik bin Anas told me, on the authority of Abu Laila bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman. Al-Ansari said that Sahl bin Abi Hathamah told him that Abdullah bin Sahl and Muhayyasah had gone to Khaybar because of a struggle that had befallen them. Then he came to Muhayyisah and was informed that Abdullah bin Sahl had been killed and thrown into a spring. The Jews came and said: By God, you killed him. They said: By God, we did not kill him. Then he approached until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that was mentioned to him. Then he himself approached. Huwayysah, who was his older brother, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl. Muhaiyysah, who was in Khaybar, went to speak. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He said “Allahu Akbar,” he said “Allahu Akbar,” and Huwayysah spoke, then Muhaiyysah spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Either you kill your friend, or you declare war, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote about that, so they wrote: By God, we did not kill him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Huwayysa, Muhaiyyah, and Abdul Rahman: Do you swear and are you entitled to the blood of your companion? They said: No. He said: Then the Jews will swear to you. They said: They are not Muslims! So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him and sent them a hundred she-camels until they entered their house. Sahl said: A red she-camel ran me over (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5778","8007 Ahmad bin Abdah told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abu Hathamah and Rafi’ bin Khadij narrated to him that Muhaiyya bin Masoud and Abdullah bin Sahl came to Khaybar in need of something. So they dispersed among the palm trees, and Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, so his brother Abdul Rahman bin Sahl, Huwaysa, and Muhaisah, his cousins, came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abdul Rahman spoke about the matter of his brother, who was younger than them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “The older one, let the older one begin. Then they talked about the matter of their companion, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said and mentioned a word that means: Fifty of you swear. They said: O Messenger of God, this is something we have not witnessed. How can we swear? He said: So the Jews will acquit you on the faith of fifty of them. They said: O Messenger of God, they are infidels, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him before him. Sahl said: So I entered a shrine for them. Then a camel of those camels gave me a gallop.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5779","5816 Qutaibah told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, he said: “A man came from Hadhramaut And a man from Kindah went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Hadrami said: O Messenger of God, “This man defeated me in a land that belonged to my father,” so he said Al-Kindi: It is my land in my hands that I cultivate. He has no right to it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have proof? He said: No. He said: His oath is upon you. He said: O Messenger of God, the man is an immoral person. He does not care about what he swore to, he is not hesitant about anything. He said: It is not yours. Other than that, he went off to swear, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when he turned back: But if he swore about his money, he would consume it unjustly. We will meet God while He is turning away from Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5780","Muhammad ibn Muammar told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Wa’il, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hijr, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when two men came to him disputing over land, and one of them said: O Messenger of God, “Indeed This one invaded my land in the pre-Islamic era, and he is Imru’ al-Qais al-Kindi, and his opponent was Rabi’ah ibn Abdan. He said: I have shown you. He said: I do not have the right to do so. Clear proof. He said: His oath. He said: Then he should take it. He said: Nothing but that. When he got up to take the oath, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He seized land unjustly, and he will meet God on the Day of Resurrection, and He will be angry with Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5781","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever swears an oath in which he is an immoral person, in order to seize the wealth of a Muslim, will meet God while He is angry with him. Al-Ash’ath said: By God, that was it. There was land between me and a Jewish man, and he denied me. So I presented it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God said to me: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do you have proof? I said: No, so he said to the Jew: Swear, so I said: By God, if he swears, my right will be gone. Then God Almighty revealed: Indeed, those who buy are with the covenant of God.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: A word of this hadith has escaped me as far as I know, and no I stand on it, and we do not know of anyone who followed Abu Muawiyah on what he said, so he said to the Jew: Swear (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5782","Al-Haytham bin Ayyub told us, he said: Yahya bin Zakaria told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: Ibn Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever swears an oath that he will take money by it while he is lying about it, he will meet God while He is angry with him, and he will be confirmed in the Book of God.” God Almighty: Indeed, those who buy God’s covenant and their oaths for a small price - those will have no share in the Hereafter. He said: Then Al-Ash’ath bin Qais came and said. : What is Abu Abdul Rahman telling you? We said: Such and such. He said: It is true. By God, it was revealed about me and so-and-so. There was a dispute between me and him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: Your witnesses or his oath. I said: Then he swears. He said: Whoever swears an oath and deducts money from it while he is a liar, will meet God and He will be upon him. Angry, so God revealed this verse.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: His follower, Mansour bin al-Mu’tamir, said:"
"5783","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Al-Ash’ath bin Qais came out against us, he said: He was between me And there was a dispute between my people, so we disputed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Whether they witness you or his oath,” so I said: Then he will swear, but not He cares, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever swears an oath to deserve money therein while in it he is an immoral person, will meet God while he is angry. Then God Almighty revealed the confirmation of that: Indeed, those who buy the covenant of God and their oaths for a small price. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5784","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: I was sent to Ibn Abbas, and I mentioned it to him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If people were given what they claim, some people would claim the blood of other men.” And their wealth, but the oath is on the defendant.” This is the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5785","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulayman told us, saying: I heard Ibn Wahb saying: Sulayman bin Bilal told me that Yahya Ibn Sa`id told him that Abu al-Zubayr told him, on the authority of Adiy ibn Adiy, on the authority of his father, who said: Two disputing men came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, in a land, and one of them said: “It is mine,” and the other said: “It is mine. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: As for whoever swears on the wealth of a Muslim, he will meet God while He is angry with him. He said: Who has abandoned it? “Paradise.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Jarir bin Hazim disagreed with him, so he came between Udayy and his father, Raja bin Haywa, and Al-Aras bin Amira. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5786","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Jarir bin Hazim, he said: I heard Adi bin Adi, speaking on the authority of Raja’ bin Haywa, And Al-Ars bin Amira, that they told him, on the authority of his father Adi bin Amira, who said: There was a dispute between Imru’ al-Qais and a man from Hadramaut. So they went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to Al-Hadrami: “I have shown you, otherwise he will take an oath.” He said: O Messenger of God, if he swears, he will go. On my land, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever swears a false oath to take away his brother’s rights by it, will meet God and He will be upon him. Angry, Imru’ al-Qais said: O Messenger of God, what is the reward for one who abandons it knowing that it is true? He said: Paradise. He said: I bear witness to you. “I have left her.” Jarir said: I was with Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani when we heard this hadith from Adiyy. Ayyoub said: Ayyub said in a hadith Al-Ars bin Amira: Then this verse was revealed: Indeed, those who buy God’s covenant and their oaths for a small price. Jarir said: And I did not remember that day. From Adi"
"5787","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Abi Al-Muthanna, the judge of Al-Masiyah, informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of An-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, “Two men claimed an animal and found it with a man, so each one stayed.” Two of them bore witness that it was his animal, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided that it should be divided into two halves.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Wrong. This Muhammad bin Kathir is Al-Musaysi, and he is truthful, except that he makes many mistakes. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Sa’id bin disagreed with him. Abu Arouba in its chain of transmission and in its text (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5788","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Ala told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Moses, that two men “disputed before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about an animal, and neither of them had proof of evidence, so he decided it between them.” “Two halves.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The chain of transmission of this hadith is good."
"5789","5826 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Two men “claimed an animal but they had no proof, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to draw their arrows on the right.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5790","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq bin Yusuf al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khalas On the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that two men negotiated a sale, and there was no evidence between them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to do so. He allowed them to make arrows on the right, whether they liked it or disliked it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5791","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Hammam bin Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, offered the people the oath, and both groups hurried to the right. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered that he participate among them in Oath, which one of them swears? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5792","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: I am Hibban, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suleiman Al-Kindi, he said: Kurdous Al-Thaalabi told us, on the authority of Al-Ash'ath bin Qais said: A man from Hadhramaut and a man from Kindah disputed before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Hadhrami said: O Messenger of God said, “My land is in the hand of this man, his father usurped it.” Al-Kindi said, “My land is in my hand and I inherited it from my father.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: Do you have proof, brother Hadhramaut? He said: No, O Messenger of God, but take his oath for me. He does not know that it is my land that his father usurped. Al-Kindi prepared to swear. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever seizes wealth with his oath will meet God with a more effective oath.” When he heard it, Al-Kindi refrained from swearing, and gave him the land.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5793","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Jesus, son of Mary, saw a man stealing. So he said to him: Did you steal? He said: No, by God, there is no god but Him. So Jesus said: I believed in God and denied my sight."
"5794","Amr bin Hisham Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: “I found Abu Jahl lying dead on the day of Badr. He said: I have a sword of mine. So I started to hit him without embarrassment, and he had his sword, so I struck his hand and the sword fell, so I took it, then I uncovered the forgiven from his head. So I beheaded him, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. He said: Is it God, besides whom there is no god? I said: Is it God, there is no god? There is no god but Him. He said: Is there Allah, besides Whom there is no god? I said: Allah, there is no god but Him. He said: Go and be firm. So I set off, and he said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If he comes to you running like a bird laughing, then he has told the truth, so I set off and was steadfast, then I came and I I run like a bird laughing. I told him, and he said: Go and show me where it is. So I went off with him and showed it to him. When the Messenger of God stopped by him, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He praised God, then said: This is the Pharaoh of this nation. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan al-Thawri disagreed with him, so he narrated it. , on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, and Abu Ubaidah did not hear from his father, and Sufyan’s narration is the correct one. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5795","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A man swore by God, ‘There is no god but He,’” was a liar. So he was forgiven.” Shu’bah said: “Before monotheism.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Sufyan disagreed with him, and he said: On the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Yahya, and he is the lame (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5796","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Samra Kufi told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: Two disputing men came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about something. He said to the plaintiff: “Provide proof.” He did not do so, and he said To the other: Swear, so he swore: By God, besides whom there is no god. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Pay his due, and it will be expiated on your behalf. There is no god but God. What you have done.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is correct, and I do not know of anyone who followed Shu’bah on what he said: On the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ubaidah On the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He said: Abu al-Ahwas followed it on its chain of transmission, and differed from it in its wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5797","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Two opponents came to the Prophet and prayed. So one of them claimed against the other, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the plaintiff: “Establish your proof.” He said: O Messenger of God, I have no Clear evidence, so he said to the other: Swear by God that there is no god but Him. He has no obligation against you or you. So he swore. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5798","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr told us, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah and Muhayyizah bin Masoud bin Zaid, they came to Khaybar, which was at that time a peace treaty, and they separated to attend to their needs. Muhayyizah came to Abdullah bin Sahl, while he was covered in the blood of a dead man, so he buried him. Then he came to Medina, and Abdul Rahman bin Sahl and Huwaisa set off. And Muhaisah went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abdul Rahman went to speak, and he was the youngest of the people in age, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “He was proud, he was proud, so I remained silent, so they spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Will you swear by fifty of you? Do you deserve your companion or your killer? They said: O Messenger of God, how can we swear when we do not bear witness and have not seen? He said: Will the Jews disavow you with fifty? They said: O Messenger of God, how can we take the oath of an infidel people? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it from him.’ Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: Saeed bin Ubaid disagreed with him regarding the meaning of the hadith."
"5799","5836 Muhammad bin Salamah, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu Laila Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Sahl, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Abi Hathamah, that he and some of the notable men of his people informed him: “That Abdullah bin Sahl and Muhaiysah went to Khaybar because of a conflict that befell them. Muhaiysah came and reported that Abdullah bin Sahl had been killed, so the Jews came and said: You killed him. They said: By God, we did not kill him. He continued until he came to his people. So he mentioned that to them, then he and his brother Huwayysah, who was older than him, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, came and went to Huwayysah. So he would speak while he was in Khaybar. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Muhaiyyasah: “Grow up.” He said “Allahu Akbar” intending to make it sound. So Huwayysah spoke, then Muhaiyyasa spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Either they will annihilate your companion, or they will announce war, so the Messenger of God wrote to them. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about that, so they wrote to him: By God, we have not killed him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Huwaisa, And Muhaisah: Do you swear, and do you deserve the blood of your companion? They said: No. He said: So will the Jews swear to you? They said: They are not Muslims. So a messenger paid tribute to him? God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came from him, so he sent them a hundred she-camels until they entered their house. Sahl said: “She ran me through her.” \red camel\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5800","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, he claimed that a man called: Sahl bin Abi Hathamah told him that: “A group of his people went to Khaybar, and they dispersed there, and they found one of them dead, so they said: To those who found him with them: You killed our companion. They said: He did not kill us, nor did we know. So they went to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Prophet of God, “We set off for Khaybar and found one of us killed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Arrogance, arrogance, and he said to them “You bring proof against whoever was killed.” They said: “We have no proof.” He said: “Then they will swear to you.” They said: “We are not satisfied with the faith of the Jews.” So he rejected it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted his blood to be shed, so he paid him one hundred camels as charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5801","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Saif, who is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “judged by oath with the witness.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is a chain of narration. Good, a trustworthy sword, and a trustworthy sword. Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan said: A trustworthy sword, and this hadith was narrated by Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Taifi, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “judged by oath with the witness,” and Muhammad bin Muslim is not that strong, and it was narrated by a weak person. He said: On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, mursal, but he has abandoned hadith, and he does not judge the weak over the trustworthy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5802","5839 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Iyad bin Himar, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever finds a piece of land, let a just person or people of justice bear witness, and then do not change or conceal it. If its Lord comes, then He has more right to it. Otherwise, it is only the property of God. He gives it to whom He wills.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5803","Ali bin Uthman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Souri told us, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “judged by oath with the witness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5804","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim bin Hashim bin Utbah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nastas, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever swears a sinful oath on my pulpit will take his seat in Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5805","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Munib bin Abdullah bin Abi Umamah bin Tha'labah, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Unais, he said: I am Abu Umamah bin Tha'labah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears a false oath at my pulpit declaring that a Muslim’s property is lawful, a curse will be upon him.” God, the angels, and all of mankind. God will not accept from him either justice or kindness.”"
"5806","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them will be a painful punishment: a stingy man who left over water on the way, preventing his son from The way is from him, and a man pledged allegiance to an imam for the sake of this world. If he gives him what he wants, he fulfills it, and if he does not give it to him, he does not fulfill it, and a man bargains with a man over his goods. After the afternoon prayer, he swore by God that he had been given such-and-such, and the other person believed him.”"
"5807","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far and Yahya told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Iyadh Abu Khaled, he said: I saw Two men were disputing at Maqil bin Yasar. Maqil said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and Yahya said: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever swears an oath by which a man’s property is taken, he will meet God while He is angry with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5808","5846 Uthman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Sahl bin Bakkar told me, he said: Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears an oath and remains patient intentionally therein is a sin.” “Whoever seizes money unjustly, then he will meet God on the Day of Resurrection, and He will be angry with Him.”"
"5809","5847 Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, it was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am only a human being.” And you dispute before me, and perhaps some of you are better off with his argument than others, so I will decide for him according to what I hear from him. I have fulfilled for him something that is due to his brother, so let him not take anything from him, for I am only granting him a portion of the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5810","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr informed us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Anas, he said: I heard Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The great sins: associating partners with God, disobeying one’s parents, killing a person, and speaking falsely.”"
"5811","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of al-Shu’bi, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Bashir, he said: My father went to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Amra bint Rawaha asked me to absolve myself, meaning: take my money from my wealth, but I refused, then it seemed to me that He let him go to him, and she said: I will not be satisfied until you go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to witness him. He said: Do you have a son other than him? “Yes.” He said: “Have you brought this to every person like the one to whom you did?” He said: “No.” He said: “I do not bear witness to this. This is unjust.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5812","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, that he heard Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, saying: He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Hassan: “Stalk them, and Gabriel is with you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5813","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, he said: Tell me Al-Baraa bin Azib said: I heard Hassan bin Thabit saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Satire them or attack them.” Meaning: the polytheists and Gabriel is with you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5814","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: Uqba bin Al-Harith bin told me Amir, that he married the daughter of Abu Ihab, and a black slave girl came and said, “I have breastfed you both.” So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, so I mentioned that to him, and he turned away. So I stepped aside and mentioned that to him, and he said: How come, when she claimed to have breastfed you both, but he forbade her? Abu Abdul Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who mentioned a black nation among those who narrated this hadith on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, other than Ibn Jurayj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5815","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Husayn told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, that he married the daughter of Abu Ihab, and a female servant from the people of Mecca came on the morning of her reign, and she said: I breastfed you both, so I asked the maid’s family, but they denied it, so I rode to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Medina. So I mentioned that to him, and I said: O Messenger of God, I asked the family of the slave girl and they denied that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How, when it was said, did he leave her, and she married someone else?"
"5816","Muhammad bin Aban Al-Balkhi and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, He said: Ubaid bin Abi Maryam told me, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, and I heard it from Uqba, but I have memorized the hadith of Ubaid. He said: I married a woman, and a black woman came and said: I have breastfed you both. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I have breastfed you both.” I married so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so, and a black woman came and said: I have breastfed you both, and she is a lie, so he turned away from me, so I went to him. On his face, I said: She is a liar. He said: How about her, when she claimed that she had breastfed you both? Leave her alone. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5817","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told us On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Amra Al Ansari, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the best of martyrs? The one who brings his testimony before... He asks her, or he informs of his testimony before he asks her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5818","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: Thana bin Abi Adiy, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrik, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, he said: “I presented Basra, then a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not Anas bin Malik. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of people. My generation, then those after them, then those after them, then there will come a fat people who are given testimony but are not asked for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5819","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God was asked God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Which of the people is best?” He said: “My generation, then those after them, then those after them, then there will come a people whose testimony will fade away.” One of them is his right hand, and his right hand dissipates his testimony.”"
"5820","5856 Ahmad bin Uthman told us, he said: Azhar told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best people are my generation, then those after them, then those after them. I do not know whether it is the fourth or the third.” He said: Then after them will be successors, the testimony of one of them will precede his oath, and his oath will be his testimony."
"5821","5857 Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, and the wording is for him, he said: Muhammad informed us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The best of you are my generation, then those after them.” Then those who follow them will succeed them, then they will be succeeded by a people whose testimonies precede their oaths, and their oaths precede their testimony.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5822","5858 Bishr bin Khalid informed us, he said: Muhammad informed us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, and Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, On the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then he will succeed me.” A people whose testimony precedes their oaths, and their oaths precede their testimony.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5823","5859 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best people are my generation, then those after them, then those after them, then he will come.” A people whose oaths precede their testimony, and their testimony precedes their oaths.”"
"5824","Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, saying: I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Fatima bint Qays “that Abu Amr bin Hafs divorced her completely while he was absent, so he sent his representative to her with barley, and she was angry with him. He said: By God, you have no charge over us. So she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him. He said: You have no maintenance. So he ordered her to observe the waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik, then he said: This is a woman who is being deceived by my companions, so perform the waiting period with the son of Umm Maktum, for he is a man. Blind man, put on your clothes, and when you undress, let me know. When I undressed, I mentioned to him that Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for Abu Jahm, he should not relieve his staff, and as for Muawiyah, he is a tramp with no money, but Marry Osama, so I married him, and God made good in him, and I was happy with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5825","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, he said: I am bin Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, and another mentioned, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa told me, Saeed, Alqamah bin Waqqas, and Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he said to her The people of Ifk did not say what they said, so God cleared them, and each of them narrated to me a group of hadith, even if some of them were more aware than others, they claimed that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for Ali bin Abi Talib and Usama bin Zaid when He delayed the revelation, consulting them about parting with his family. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with someone who knew who The innocence of his family, and with what was in his heart to respond to them, so he said: O Messenger of God, your family, and we know nothing but good. As for Ali, he said: O Messenger of God, God has not made it difficult for you, and there are many women besides her, and if you ask a slave girl, she will tell you the truth. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed He greeted Barirah and said: “O Barirah, have you seen anything that made you suspicious?” Barirah said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen anything wrong with her. “I will make him feel sad for her, more than that, because she is a young girl who sleeps while watching her family’s dough, and the domestic animal comes and eats it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5826","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, that Zaid Abu Ayyash told him Saad said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, being asked about buying dates with dates. He said: Do dates decrease when they are dry? They said: Yes, so he forbade it."
"5827","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan, who is Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “He entered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was pleased with me one day, and he said: O Aisha, did you not see that Mujazza al-Mudaliji entered upon me and was with me? Osama bin Zaid. He saw Osama and Zaid wearing velvet, and they covered their heads and their feet were visible, so he said: These are feet one of the other.” Sufyan said: This is the strengthening of the Qafah."
"5828","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am al-Thawri, on the authority of Saleh al-Hamdani, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, who said: “Three people were brought to Ali while he was in Yemen, and they had sexual intercourse with a woman who was in the same period of purity, so he asked two of them: Do they marry each other? Meaning: for this man with the child. They said: No. Then he asked two of them: Will you marry this man with the child? They said: No. So he cast lots among them, and he decided that the child would go to him. The lot was cast upon him, and two-thirds of the blood money was imposed upon him. I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed until his molars were visible.” Ishaq bin Shaheen told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of a man from Hadhramaut, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Ali to Yemen, and he brought a boy over whom three people quarreled. Al-Marwazi, he said: I am Ali bin Mushari, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Khalil Al-Hadrami informed me, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from the people of Yemen came and began to inform him and talk to him.” He mentioned the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5829","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Baqiyya bin Al-Walid, he said: Buhair bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Jubayr. Ibn Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, said: “The Ansar cast lots among their houses as to which of them would shelter the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Ayyub defeated them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took refuge in him. Whenever gifts were given to him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Food that he sent to us.” A summary. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Buhair bin Sa’d is trustworthy."
"5830","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn al-Harith, told us. Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard Al-Numan bin Bashir said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The lawful is clear, and the forbidden is clear, and there are matters in between that.” Suspected matters, he said: And perhaps he said: And among that are suspicious matters, and I will give you an example in that: Indeed, God protected, and indeed, God protected. What is forbidden, and whoever grazes around a fever is about to come into contact with a fever, and perhaps he said: He who grazes around a fever is about to come into contact with a fever. In it, and whoever is mixed with doubt is about to dare.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5831","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A time will come upon the people, when a man will not care where he got the money from, whether he got it, or \Forbidden\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5832","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, who is Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Khaira, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There will come a time when people will consume usury, so whoever does not consume it, He was struck by his dust.”"
"5833","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of His paternal aunt, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best thing a man eats is from his own earnings, and a man’s offspring is from \Earn it\"""""""
"5834","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of a paternal aunt of his, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your children are among the best of your earnings, so eat of your children’s earnings.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5835","Yusuf bin Issa Al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best thing a man eats is from his own earnings, and his children are from his earnings.”"
"5836","Ahmad bin Hafs told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best thing a man eats is from his own earnings. And his child is from his earnings.” Suleiman said: Amara bin Umair told me, on the authority of his paternal aunt, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar."
"5837","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibn Jarir told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Amr bin Taghlib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of the signs of the Hour is that money will increase and increase, trade will spread, and ignorance will appear.” And the man sells the item, and says: “Until I seek advice from a merchant of so-and-so.” And the clerk is sought in the great neighborhood, but he is not found."
"5838","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two parties are at option as long as they do not separate. If they tell the truth and make it clear, they will be blessed in their sale, but if they lie and conceal it, the blessing of their sale is due.”"
"5839","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Kharshah bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three whom God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them.” And He will not purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it, and Abu Dharr said: They were disappointed and lost. He said: “Al-Musbil His garment is vanity, the spender’s goods are his false oaths, and the generous is his giving.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5840","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Sulayman al-Amash told me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Mushar, On the authority of Kharshah ibn al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There are three whom God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purifies them, and for them is a painful punishment: He who gives nothing except as a gift, and he who sends his burden on the way, and he who spends his goods by lying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5841","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “An oath is one that is spent for the sake of one’s goods, and one that is one that is one that destroys one’s gain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5842","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-Walid, meaning Ibn Kathir, told me on the authority of Ma’abad bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Qatada Al-Ansari, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Beware of swearing too much when selling; “It spends, then it is paid back.”"
"5843","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, he said: “There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them will be a painful punishment: a man who was miserly who left the water on the way, A wayfarer is prevented from it. A man pledged allegiance to an imam for the sake of this world. If he gives him what he wants, he fulfills it. If he does not give it to him, he does not fulfill it. And a man bargains. A man received a commodity after the afternoon prayer, and he swore to him by God that he had been given such-and-such, and the other believed him.”"
"5844","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abi Wael, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Gharza, he said: We were In Medina, we buy and sell merchandise, and we call ourselves brokers, and the people call us. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us. So he gave us a name that is better for us than the one by which we called ourselves, and said: “O merchants, your selling is witnessed by swearing and idle talk. They tinged it with charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5845","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Al-Harith, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Hakim Ibn Hazzam, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two parties are at option as long as they do not separate. “And if they are clear and truthful, they will be blessed in their sale, and if they lie and conceal it, then the blessing of their sale is due.”"
"5846","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two parties who pledge allegiance, each one of them With the option on its owner, as long as they do not separate, except selling the option.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5847","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “The sale is at option as long as they do not separate, or it is an option.”"
"5848","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb told us, he said: Mahrez bin Al-Wadah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two parties who sell each other are at option, unless they separate, unless the sale is at option. \An option"
"5849","Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Nafi’ dictated to me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If two parties sell each other, each one of them has the option of selling it, unless they separate, or their sale is “For an option. If it was for an option, then the sale is obligatory.”"
"5850","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sale is for option unless they separate, or he says: Choose.”"
"5851","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The sale is for option until they separate, or it is a sale of option, and perhaps Nafi’ said: Or one of them says to the other: Select \"" 5852"""""
"5852","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: ""When two men transact a sale, each of them has the option (to cancel) until they separate."" And he said on another occasion: ""As long as they have not separated, and they are together, or one of them gives the other the option; if one gives the other the option and they transact on that basis, the sale becomes binding. And if they separate after transacting, and neither of them abandons the sale, the sale becomes binding."""""
"5853","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed, saying: I heard Nafi’, speaking on the authority of Ibn Omar. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The two parties to the transaction have the option of selling each other as long as they do not separate, unless the sale is voluntary.” Nafi’ said: Whenever Abdullah bin Omar bought something he liked, he would leave its owner."
"5854","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no sale between the two parties until they separate, except for the sale of options.”"
"5855","Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For every sale there is no sale between them until they separate, except for the sale of options.”"
"5856","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Every two sales, there is no sale between them until they separate, except the sale of options.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5857","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad Al-Harrani told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no sale between any two sales until they separate, except for the sale of options.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5858","Amr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Bahz bin Asad, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every two sales, there is no sale between them until they separate, except the sale of options.”"
"5859","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Every two sellers, there is no sale between them.” Until they separate, except for selling the option.”"
"5860","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The sale is for option unless they separate, or their sale is for option.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5861","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Prophet God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The sale is at option until they separate, or each one of them takes from the sale what he likes.” And they choose three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5862","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sale is at option as long as they do not separate, or one of them takes what he pleases from his owner and does not \He is\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5863","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two parties bargain by option unless they separate, unless it is an option deal, and it is not permissible for him to He leaves his companion for fear that he will resign him.”"
"5864","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said that he was being deceived in the sale, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “When you give the pledge of allegiance, say: No deception.” And when the man sold He says: No wonder"
"5865","Yusuf bin Hammad told us, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that a man had a weakness in his contract, He was pledging allegiance, and his family came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Prophet of God, quarantine him, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, summoned him. He greeted him, but he forbade him and said: O Prophet of God, I am not patient with the sale. He said: “If you sell, say: No confusion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5866","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: he told me Abu Kathir said that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you sells a sheep, or a \He celebrates it\"""""""
"5867","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Do not meet the riders to sell, and do not drive camels or sheep. Whoever buys any of these things will have the best of both worlds, if he wishes.” He kept it, and if he wanted to return it, he could return it and with it a saa’ of dates, not brown ones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5868","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Dawud bin Qays told me, on the authority of Ibn Yasar, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever buys an espresso, if he is satisfied with it when he milks it, let him keep it, even if he is satisfied with it when he milks it. He disliked it, so let him return it with a saa’ of dates.”"
"5869","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: Abu said Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever buys a caravan or a caravan, he has the option for three days. If he wishes to keep it, he can keep it. And if he wants to return it, he can return it with a cup of dates, not a brown one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5870","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, and Waki’, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Mukhlid bin Khafaf, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that the tax is subject to guarantee.”"
"5871","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the receipt of goods, and for an immigrant to sell to a Bedouin, and the transfer of goods, Najsh, and for a man to bargain for his brother’s price, and for a woman to ask for her sister’s divorce. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5872","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: Muhammad bin al-Zabarqan told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He forbade selling a slave to a slave, even if it was his father and brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5873","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Salem bin Nuh told me, he said: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “We were forbidden from selling a slave to a slave, even if it was his brother or father.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Salim ibn Nuh is not strong, and Muhammad ibn al-Zabarqan is more beloved to us than him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5874","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “ “We are forbidden from selling a present to a distant person.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5875","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, that he heard Jabir, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A present person should not sell to a stranger. Leave the people, and God will provide for them, some of them from others.”"
"5876","Qutayba bin Sa`id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Do not meet riders to sell, and do not sell to one another, and do not quarrel, and do not sell one present to another.”"
"5877","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam ibn Ayan told me, saying: Shuaib ibn al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on many Ibn Farqad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he “forbade intercourse, meeting people, and selling ever-present\"" 5878"""""
"5878","'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade talqqi (meeting caravans outside the market to buy goods before they reach the market)."
"5879","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I told Abu Usama: Ubayd Allah told you, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about receiving the baggage until he enters the market with it. Abu Usama acknowledged this and said: Yes."
"5880","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the possession of riders, and the selling of a living person to a lost person.” I said to Ibn Abbas: What is his saying: A present person does not sell to a lost person? They said: He does not have a broker (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5881","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Juraij said: he said: Hisham Al-Qurdousi informed us He heard Ibn Sirin say: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not face the tribulation, for whoever receives it... So he bought from him, and when his master comes to the market, he will have the option.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5882","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A present man shall not sell to a stranger, nor shall they quarrel with him, nor shall a man bargain for the same amount as his brother, nor shall he propose to another.” Proposing to his brother, and a woman should not ask for a divorce from her sister so that she may be content with what is in her vessel, and so that she may be married, for she only gets what God has decreed for her.”"
"5883","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Layth, and the wording is his, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “None of you should sell on the basis of selling to others.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5884","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not sell as his brother sells, until he buys or leaves.”"
"5885","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade defilement.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5886","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: He told me Abu Salamah and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A man should not sell for the sake of selling something.” He should not sell his brother, nor should he sell a slave, nor should they quarrel, nor should a man propose to his brother after his brother’s engagement, nor should a woman ask for another’s divorce, so that she may be content with it. whatever is in its vessel” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5887","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A person who is present should not sell to a stranger, and do not quarrel, and a man should not add to his brother’s sale, and do not ask “The woman divorced her sister, so that she could make use of what was on her record as sufficient for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5888","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, and Issa bin Yunus told us, they said: Al-Akhdar bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr. Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sold a cup and a cup of tea, so who can do more?”"
"5889","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Touching and repulsiveness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5890","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. He said: Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Touching: touching the garment without looking at it, and about Munabadha: which is a man offering his garment to another man for sale, before he turns it around, or He looks at him"
"5891","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus told me On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade touching. And competition in selling.”"
"5892","Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two transactions: touching each other and fighting each other.”"
"5893","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa ibn Bahloul told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Harb, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Sa`id, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade confrontation and touching, and touching means that two men should pledge allegiance.” With two garments at night, each man touches the other’s garment with his hand. Al-Munabdha: for one man to throw the garment over to another. The other will give him the garment, and they will agree on that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5894","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Aamir bin Saad told him that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade touching, and touching means touching a garment. He does not look at it, and about Munabadha, and Munabadha: A man throws his garment to another man, before he turns it inside out.”"
"5895","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two dresses and two sales. As for the two sales: touching, Al-Munabdhah, Al-Munabdhah: for a man to say: If I reject this garment, then it is obligatory, meaning sale, and touching: for him to touch it. With his hand, and he does not spread it or turn it over, if he touches it, it is obligatory to sell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5896","Harun bin Zaid bin Abi Al-Zarqa told us about Ramla, he said: My father told us, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan told us, he said: He informed me about, Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade two types of clothing, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us.” He said hello to two transactions: the contract and the touch, which were transactions they used to trade in during pre-Islamic times. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and Ja`far bin Burqan is not strong in al-Zuhri in particular, and in other matters there is nothing wrong with him, and likewise Sufyan bin Hussein and Suleiman bin Kathir"
"5897","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Khubayb, who is Ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that “he forbade two transactions, and as for the two transactions, they are rebellious, And touching, and he claimed that touching is when a man says to another man: I will sell you my dress for yours, and neither of them looks at the other’s dress. But he touches him a little, and as for the rejection: he says: I reject what I have, and you reject what you have. He buys one of them from the other, and he does not know each of them. \One of them as well as the other.\"" And something similar to this description"
"5898","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa`id told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Abu al-Zinad informed me, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the selling of pebble, and the selling of deception.”"
"5899","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “No “Sell the fruit until its goodness appears.” He forbade the seller and the buyer."
"5900","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace \"" 5901"""""
"5901","Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed me, reading to him while I listened, from Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Sa'id and Abu Salamah narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not sell fruit until its ripeness becomes apparent, and do not sell fruit for dried dates."" Ibn Shihab said: Salim ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade... the like of it exactly."
"5902","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, he said: Hanzalah told us, he said: I heard a peacock, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us and said: “Do not sell the fruit until its goodness appears.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5903","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, talking about The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade communicating with each other, trading, and competing with one another, and that the fruit should be sold until its goodness appears, and that It is sold only for dinars and dirhams, and it is licensed in Al-Arayya. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5904","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He forbade communicating with one another, trading with one another, competing with one another, and selling fruit until it feeds anyone but the naked. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5905","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him about selling palm trees until they are fed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5906","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling fruits until they were ripe. It was said: Oh"
"5907","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, that he heard Jabir, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you sell fruit to your brother, and a pestilence strikes him, it is not permissible for you to take any of it from him. “You take your brother’s money unlawfully?”"
"5908","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, he said: Thawr bin Yazid told us, that he heard Ibn Juraij, speaking On the authority of Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells fruit, then A pandemic, so he should not take it from his brother, and he mentioned something: Why should one of you eat his Muslim brother’s wealth?"
"5909","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Sulayman bin Ateeq, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, “the situation of pandemics” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5910","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Iyaad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man was injured in the fruits he had bought, and his debt increased. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They gave him alms, and the people gave alms to him, but that did not amount to the fulfillment of his debt, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take what you find. And you have nothing but that.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more valid than the hadith of Suleiman bin Atiq."
"5911","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Araj, on the authority of Sulayman bin Atik, Qutaibah said: Atik Sufficiently, and what is correct is Atiq. On the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of fruit for years.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5912","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade Concerning the sale of fruit for dates, “Ibn Umar said: Zaid bin Thabit told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “authorized the sale of naked women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5913","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. “He forbade the muzabanah, and the muzabanah: that what is on the tops of palm trees is sold for dates for a specified measure. If there is more, then yes, and if there is less. \On me\"""""""
"5914","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade It means about the Muzabanah, and the Muzabanah: selling the fruit for dates by the measure, and selling the vineyard for the price of raisins by the measure.”"
"5915","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the practice of competition and competition.”"
"5916","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: Zayd bin Thabit told me, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “granted permission to be naked.”"
"5917","Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read to him, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: He told me outside Ibn Zayd Ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “allowed dates and fresh dates to be given to private women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5918","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Zayd bin It is established that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “granted the sale of naked women, to be sold separately.”"
"5919","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Zayd bin Thabit told me, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “granted the sale of a female slave by giving her dates as dates.”"
"5920","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Salim He told him that he heard Abdullah bin Omar say: Zayd bin Thabit told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, authorized the sale of He gave the naked dates and dates, and he did not permit anything other than that.”"
"5921","Ishaq bin Mansour and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud bin Husayn, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “allowed, in the case of naked women, to be sold for a sum of five \Awsaq"
"5922","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abu Hathamah said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the sale of fruit until its goodness appears, and he permitted the sale of naked fruits at their pure price.” Its people eat it fresh.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5923","Al-Hussein bin Issa told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told me, he said: Bashir bin Yasar told me, Rafi’ bin Khadij and Sahl bin Abi Hathamah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade muzabanah: selling fruit for dates, except for owners of naked people, for He has permitted them.”"
"5924","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, that they said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for the sale of naked women for a price.”"
"5925","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Saad, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about fresh dates, and he said to those around him: ‘Does the fresh date decrease? When it dries up? They said: Yes, so he forbade it."
"5926","Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, On the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Saad bin Malik, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about fresh dates with dates, and he said: ‘Does it decrease when it dries? He said: Yes, so he forbade it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5927","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubair told me, that he heard Jabir bin Abd God, says: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the sale of dates, without knowing its measure in terms of the designated measure of dates.”"
"5928","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu Al-Zubair told me, that he heard Jabir bin Abd God, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A grain of food is not sold for a grain of food, nor a grain of food for the specified measure of food.” \the food called\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5929","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Al-Muzabanah: To sell the fruit of his garden, even if it is a palm tree, for a measure of dates, and if it is a vineyard, to sell it for a measure of raisins, or if it is crops, To sell it for a measure of food, he forbade all of that.”"
"5930","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he is Ibn Yazid, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade communicating with each other, exchanging business, and competing with one another, and selling the fruit before it was eaten, and Sell that except for dinars and dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5931","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “About communicating with one another, trading with one another, and engaging in competition, and selling fruit until it is fed, except for the naked.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5932","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said, “He forbade the sale of the palm tree until it flourished, and of the corn until it turned white and was free from defect. He forbade the seller and the buyer.”"
"5933","Qutaibah bin Saeed narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Salih, that a man One of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed him. He said: O Messenger of God, we do not find Al-Sayhani nor Al-Athq collecting dates, even We will increase them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sell it for paper money, then buy it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5934","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a recitation of it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Suhail, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He appointed a man to Khaybar, and he brought some rare dates. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Eat the dates of Khaybar.” Like this? He said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, we will take one saa’ of this for two saa’s, and two saa’s for three, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not do that. Sell the lot for dirhams, then buy for dirhams separately.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5935","Nasr bin Ali and Ismail bin Masoud told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with ripe dates, and the dates of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, were brought He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, greeted Baala, who had something dry in it. He said: “How did you get this?” They said: “We bought it one sa’ for two sa’s of our dates.” He said: “Do not do it. This is not appropriate, but sell your dates and buy what you need from this.”"
"5936","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abu Sa`id al-Khudri told me, he said: We were provided with the dates of the masses during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we sell two saa’s for another saa’, and that was conveyed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “There is no saa’ of dates for a saa’, and no saa’ of wheat for a saa’, nor “One dirham for two dirhams”"
"5937","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah told me, he said: Abu Sa’id told me, He said: We used to sell a group of dates, two sa's for a sa', and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not give a sa' of dates for a sa', nor do I give a sa' of wheat for a sa', nor do \Two dirhams for one dirham\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5938","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Hamza, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: He told me Uqba bin Abdul Ghafir said: Abu Sa’id told me, he said: Bilal came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some dates, and he said: “What This one? He said: I bought it one saa’ for two saa’s. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh, it is usury, do not approach it.”"
"5939","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan, that he heard Omar bin Al-Khattab says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Gold means usury by paper, except for Ha and Ha, and righteousness for righteousness is usury. Except Ha and Ha, and barley for barley is usury, except Ha and ha, and dates for dates is usury, except Ha and ha.”"
"5940","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt hand in hand. So whoever adds or It increased, but it increased, except for what its colors differed.”"
